<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  What the app is allowed to do under the hardened runtime.

  Hardened runtime is not optional here: it is one of the three conditions a macOS build has
  to meet before Apple's notary service will look at it — a Developer ID certificate, a
  timestamp, and the hardened runtime option (the same three `packaging/make-pkg.mjs` names).
  It is also restrictive in a way V8 cannot live with.

  **`allow-jit`** is the one that matters: the renderer is V8, V8 compiles JavaScript to
  machine code while it runs, and under the hardened runtime that memory is not executable
  unless this key says it is. Without it the window opens and then dies on the first script
  the page runs, which is a failure that only appears in a *signed* build — every unsigned
  build this project has ever made ran fine without it.

  **`allow-unsigned-executable-memory`** is V8's other path to the same need (it writes code
  into a buffer it allocated itself rather than into a mapping it asked to be executable).

  **`disable-library-validation`** lets the app load the frameworks inside its own bundle
  without each one having been signed by the same team in the same process; the helpers
  Electron spawns are signed with these same entitlements, which is what
  `entitlementsInherit` in `ui/package.json` is for.

  Nothing here is broader than what a stock Electron build already declares — this file exists
  so the answers live in the repository, where the packaging test can read them, rather than
  inside electron-builder's defaults.

  **One thing must stay out of this file: two hyphens in a row, comments included.** XML
  forbids that sequence inside a comment, and the parser `codesign` uses refuses the entire
  file with "AMFIUnserializeXML: syntax error near line N" — while `plutil -lint` still
  answers OK, so the mistake passes the obvious check and surfaces only on the release
  runner, at the moment signing starts. It was made once here (a flag was written out in
  full inside this comment) and measured: `ui/electron/packaging.test.mjs` now pins the rule.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
